  "description": "MEJVII crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C199 H140 Dy14 N56 O66 5+,2.5(C1 O3 2-),0.5(C12 H8 N2),26(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy13 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy14 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.746-4.813 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.92-157.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy14(CO3)13(ccnm)10(OH)(H2O)6(phen)13](CO3)2.5·(phen)0.5·26H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
